	ida_struct.set_member_cmt(ida_struct.get_member(struc, 128784), '''String: "Detailed explanation of why hashrate amounts may change over time"''', True)
	ida_struct.set_member_cmt(ida_struct.get_member(struc, 128776), '''String: "From time to time we may adjust the hashrate amounts available for free, rewarded, or paid plans to keep the system sustainable and aligned with real Bitcoin network conditions, advertising revenue, capacity, and other factors. When demand or costs increase, the in-app cost of hashrate may rise, so for the same price (or via free/rewarded plans) you may receive less hashrate than before.\n\nIf the hashrate offered for watching ads seems lower after many ads in a row, this may be due to how ad partners, pacing, and our anti-abuse/operational limits allocate rewards. Taking a break and trying again later may result in a different offer.\n\nWhen conditions are more favorable, we may be able to offer higher hashrate at the same or lower in-app cost.\n\nOnce you purchase or claim a free/rewarded plan, the hashrate shown for that plan remains same for its active duration, even if future offers change. However, reward outcomes remain variable and are not guaranteed.\n\n"''', True)
	ida_struct.set_member_cmt(ida_struct.get_member(struc, 128768), '''String: "Help modal title explaining hashrate changes"''', True)
